		For style: inner
			Box:
				Margin: 0
			For element: Cell
				Box:
					Padding: 2 4
					Border: 0 0 0.5 0
					Border color: rule
	Section:
		Text: Tables
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Elements in a cell
		Paragraph: A `Cell` with a value is one text. Without a value it is a block with its elements, one below another, or nothing. Here the cells take `Trim margins: both` from a rule, so the margins of the first and the last paragraph do not leave a gap inside the cell.
